# RGJ-B6-002..006 — consolidated lifecycle integration specification
#
# Libretro.java target integration
# -------------------------------
# Startup, after target environment/protocol streams are valid:
#     RG35XXLifecycle.platformStart();
#
# Immediately before platform.load(game) / case 10 new-game path:
#     RG35XXLifecycle.beforeGameLoad();
#
# MIDlet pause/destroy boundaries where the libretro facade owns the event:
#     RG35XXLifecycle.pauseBarrier();
#     RG35XXLifecycle.destroyBarrier();
#
# Game unload/replacement:
#     RG35XXLifecycle.unloadGame();
# This must occur before discarding the old MobilePlatform/MIDlet state.
#
# Final Java shutdown:
#     RG35XXLifecycle.platformShutdown();
# Do not separately reorder RMS/audio teardown around it.
#
# IMPORTANT: RG35XXAudioBootstrap attachment still happens only after the
# inherited dedicated FD property is available. Lifecycle coordinates reset and
# shutdown; it does not manufacture the inherited descriptor.
#
# freej2me_libretro.c target integration
# --------------------------------------
# retro_load_game / Java process setup:
#   1. init media cache + mixer/event callback
#   2. create dedicated audio pipe
#   3. fork JamVM
#   4. parent closes write end; child closes read end
#   5. child receives -Dfreej2me.rg35xx.audio.fd=<write_fd>
#   6. parent audio worker drains pipe independently of retro_run
#
# game RESET command:
#   mixer_reset() BEFORE media_cache_reset().
#
# retro_unload_game:
#   allow Java lifecycle unload/reset to complete before destroying process-owned
#   resources. Do not kill a live Java child before its RMS force-flush barrier.
#
# retro_deinit final ordering:
#   request/observe Java shutdown where current core protocol permits;
#   stop worker ownership;
#   close audio pipe;
#   reset mixer;
#   reset/free media cache;
#   destroy remaining synchronization objects.
#
# Preserved invariants
# --------------------
# - stdout stays binary video IPC; never redirect it for logs/audio.
# - fixed frontend geometry remains 640x480 RGB565.
# - receiver pthread and async audio callback/ring remain independent of retro_run.
# - no 3-second/aggressive watchdog.
# - native MIDI END_OF_MEDIA remains authoritative.
# - old SD audio bridge remains rollback-only until consolidated device pass.
